// ?Rva0052AE20@@YAHH@Z
// partial score=0.8442 date=2026-09-29
// cl: /DNDEBUG /MD /EHsc

// Identity: an address-keyed free function, `int __cdecl(int)`. The matched
// caller bfmeProvideObjectiveStatus (0x0052AE80, BfmeAptScreenObjectivesProvide.cpp)
// pushes one dword, caller-cleans with `add esp,4` and tests the result as a
// signed int, so the ledger's `?d_0052ae20@@YAXXZ` (void, no argument) is
// contradicted; see targets/game/reverse/identity_evidence/0052ae20-abi.md.
// No Zero Hour twin and no vtable slot name it, so the address token stays.
//
// WHAT THIS SHAPE FIXES (measured, 2026-09-29). Ten earlier sessions could not
// stop MSVC 7.1 inverting the loop: every `for`/`while (i < count)`/`goto`
// spelling became a guarded do-while with the compare duplicated into the
// latch (79 bytes). Writing the loop as `while ( flag )` with the count test
// as an early return at the top of the body keeps ONE shared header compare,
// the 2-byte back jump, and the lazy `push edi` after the count call, exactly
// as retail has it, and lands on 77 bytes. The matched body
// GameTextManager::reverseWord (0x00435F70) is the repo's proof that this
// spelling is reachable: `while (ok)` with `if (file >= lp) return;` compiles
// top-tested there.
//
// WHAT IS STILL WRONG. Twelve of 77 bytes: the parameter (`n`) and the
// objective count swap between EBX and EBP. Everything else, including the
// loop shape, the block layout and the epilogue, is byte-exact.
//
// MEASURED THIS SESSION (2026-09-29, second pass on the residue; the harness
// is build/scratch/try.py and the variants are build/scratch/reg*.cpp):
//
// 1. The allocation follows the count's FIRST USE, not the copy's position.
//    Whenever the count is first zero-tested, the entry-block copy takes EBP
//    and the count takes EBX -- retail's map. Two independent spellings show
//    it, and both are 12+ bytes over only because of that extra test:
//      * d1 (`if ( count == 0 ) return -1;` before the flag loop) compiles the
//        first 30 bytes byte-for-byte retail, including `push ebp / mov
//        ebp,[esp+8] / jne / or eax,-1 / pop ebp / ret / push ebx / push esi /
//        call / mov ebx,eax / xor esi,esi`, at 93 bytes;
//      * w0_goto (the goto form, which the compiler rotates) peels the header
//        test into `test ebx,ebx / jle` and likewise gets EBP/EBX, at 79.
//    When the count's first use is the header `cmp esi,ebx`, the copy takes
//    EBX -- every flag-loop spelling measured. The zero test itself cannot be
//    free: it needs a second -1 exit path (EDI is not saved yet at +0x1F), so
//    d1 costs 16 bytes and `while ( count )` (f1) 11. An empty then-body
//    (`if (count == 0) { }`) is deleted and flips nothing.
//
// 2. An incoming ARGUMENT and a local copy of it allocate differently, and
//    their register copies are placed differently. Used directly, `n` gets EBP
//    (retail's register) but its copy is materialised at +0x16, just after the
//    count call, not at +0x09: an argument live across a call is copied into
//    its callee-saved register after that call (measured: with no call before
//    the loop the same copy lands at the top of the then-block, +0x0E). A
//    local's store stays at its definition point, which is what puts the copy
//    in the entry block -- but a local takes EBX. So neither spelling alone
//    can be retail: the one with retail's copy slot has EBX, the one with
//    retail's registers copies late.
//
// 3. Ruled out by measurement this session, all 77 or 93 bytes, none exact:
//    flag declared before the copy, flag as int/char/pointer/from-the-count/
//    cleared-on-exit/reassigned-in-the-loop; dead stores for count, cursor or
//    current ahead of the copy; one- and two-variable declaration lists;
//    count-first through a ternary (93 B, the guard does not fold);
//    unsigned, long, register-qualified and const locals; break, continue,
//    goto, do-while and flag-entry-branch mixes; the count call written inside
//    the loop for LICM (86 B); goto back edges behind an opaque flag guard
//    (still rotates, 79 B).

class CampaignManager
{
public:
	int getMissionObjectiveCount();
	bool isMissionObjectiveEligible( int index );
};

typedef CampaignManager Glo012F1028Type;

extern Glo012F1028Type *Glo012F1028;

// The campaign singleton at 0x012F1028 is typed
// ?TheLivingWorldLogic@@3PAVCampaignManager@@A in symbols.csv; the objective
// count and eligibility predicates are ILT 0x0002A62B and 0x00039A77.
int Rva0052AE20( int n )
{
	int remain = n;

	if ( Glo012F1028 == 0 )
		return -1;

	// A flag loop rather than `for (cursor = 0; cursor < count; ++cursor)`:
	// MSVC 7.1 inverts the counted form and duplicates the compare into the
	// latch, which is the whole 79-versus-77 byte gap. See the header.
	bool more = true;
	int count = Glo012F1028->getMissionObjectiveCount();
	int cursor = 0;
	int current;

	while ( more )
	{
		if ( cursor >= count )
			return -1;

		current = cursor++;

		if ( !Glo012F1028->isMissionObjectiveEligible( current ) )
			continue;

		if ( remain <= 0 )
			return current;

		--remain;
	}
}
